      "why": "Reports the actual fan-out numbers behind the deep research loop."
    },
    {
      "text": "For the course, it worked great right away. We generated 35 lessons really quick, but we wanted more.",
      "timestamp_sec": 925,
      "why": "Quantifies what V1 actually delivered before they scaled ambition."
    },
    {
      "text": "this research MD file is static. It's a pile of static data. And usually research is not static, right?",
      "timestamp_sec": 1063,
      "why": "The motivation for adding the wiki layer."
    },
    {
      "text": "It consumes a lot of tokens and it takes a lot of time.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1063,
      "why": "Names the cost that makes persistence necessary."
    },
    {
      "text": "that's why V3 of this system is actually a deep research algorithm plus an LM knowledge base on top of it, aka the wiki layer.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1100,
      "why": "One-sentence definition of the final architecture."
    },
    {
      "text": "you should forget the infra structure you think you need, such as vector databases, knowledge graphs, semantic search, text search.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1144,
      "why": "The most contrarian claim in the talk."
    },
    {
      "text": "So, no database, just a simple index based on references.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1185,
      "why": "The design decision stated at its most compressed."
    },
    {
      "text": "And sometimes the agent just looks into this, gets what it needs, and goes back. Which is very token efficient, right?",
      "timestamp_sec": 1371,
      "why": "Explains why the summary hierarchy pays off."
    },
    {
      "text": "the beautiful part is that this wiki is actually alive, right? For example, every question leaves a trace into your wiki.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1418,
      "why": "The idea that distinguishes this from a static research artifact."
    },
    {
      "text": "Obsidian is just an immutable snapshot that a LLM never touches, right? So, this is my data. I don't really want the LLM to touch my personal notes that I manually write",
      "timestamp_sec": 1499,
      "why": "A firm boundary between human-authored source and machine-generated derivative."
    },
    {
      "text": "The project is the work, and your second brain is the research.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1596,
      "why": "The organizing metaphor for how scoping works."
    },
    {
      "text": "usually light or fast is more than enough because remember this process consumes a lot of tokens.",
      "timestamp_sec": 1723,
      "why": "Practical operating guidance with a stated cost reason."
    },
    {
      "text": "the other main goal of this project is to teach memory and context management",
      "timestamp_sec": 2222,
      "why": "Explains why missing connectors are not treated as bugs."
    },
    {
      "text": "our goal is to teach AI engineering. It's not to build the next best product.",
      "timestamp_sec": 2257,
      "why": "Sets expectations for anyone considering adopting the repo."
